Ensuring secure, auditable scientific computation.

Representative Scenario

A typical APP‑SE run models a 10–20 MeV proton source accelerated by a 35 fs, 800 nm, (3 \times 10^{19}) W/cm² laser pulse inside a star‑forming molecular cloud environment. Outputs include thrust formation, beam stability, cosmic‑field modulation, and nozzle performance.

Scientific Impact

APP‑SE establishes a new class of propulsion simulation instrument that merges astrophysics, plasma physics, and engine dynamics. It enables exploration of proton propulsion concepts shaped by the physical structure of the universe, supporting future research in high‑specific‑impulse, field‑controlled propulsion systems.

